  "faq_h2": "Discord symbols, answered",
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Do you need Nitro to use Discord symbols?",
      "a": "No. The symbols on this page are standard Unicode characters, so they work on every Discord account, free or Nitro. Nitro adds custom and animated emoji, bigger uploads, and profile extras, but text symbols and Unicode fonts never require it. (See Discord allowed characters for field-by-field rules.)"
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I add symbols to my Discord name or bio?",
      "a": "Click any symbol to copy it, then paste it into your Discord display name, About Me, server nickname, server name, or a message. Note that the login username field only allows lowercase letters, numbers, underscores, and periods: symbols go in the display name, not the username."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I use symbols in Discord channel names?",
      "a": "Yes, partially. Channel names are lowercased and spaces become hyphens, but many Unicode symbols and dividers (such as ⊹, ➤, │, and ⌗) work as prefixes or separators to organise a server's channel list and categories. Test on desktop and mobile, since support can vary."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do some Discord symbols show as blank boxes?",
      "a": "A blank box means the viewer's device or app version has no glyph for that character. Widely supported symbols (stars, hearts, dots, box-drawing dividers) render almost everywhere; rarer characters may not. If a symbol looks broken for others, swap it for a more common alternative."
    }
  ],
